1.34.m:
Cyavana said:
"This very thing will surely come to pass, which you ask of me, O king;
the status of a brahmin will belong to you through the lineage following our lineage.

1.35.m:
Sūrya said:
"This is my inherent nature, O brahmin, that my essence is heat;
and since I act according to my nature, you ought not to be angry with me.

1.40.m:
Rāhu said:
Enmity with the all-powerful Viṣṇu does not please me,
from whose wrath I was born without a body, the crusher of the enemy's host,

The Holy One said:
O thirty [gods], you ought to make an effort in churning the Ocean of Milk;
joined with the dānavas, you will then attain the highest good.

1.47.m:
Mārkaṇḍeya said:
Adorned with a matted coil of hair resembling the color of fire flames,
as if the sun's orb in summer had mounted half the sky;
